{"id":"CVE-2020-12062","lastModified":"2026-10-14T10:17:25.737","vulnStatus":"Modified","descriptions":[{"lang":"en","value":"The scp client in OpenSSH 8.2 incorrectly sends duplicate responses to the server upon a utimes system call failure, which allows a malicious unprivileged user on the remote server to overwrite arbitrary files in the client's download directory by creating a crafted subdirectory anywhere on the remote server. The victim must use the command scp -rp to download a file hierarchy containing, anywhere inside, this crafted subdirectory. NOTE: the vendor points out that \"this attack can achieve no more than a hostile peer is already able to achieve within the scp protocol\" and \"utimes does not fail under normal circumstances."}],"metrics":{"cvssMetricV31":[{"type":"Primary","cvssData":{"baseScore":7.5,"baseSeverity":"HIGH","vectorString":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:N"}}],"cvssMetricV2":[{"type":"Primary","cvssData":{"baseScore":5,"vectorString":"AV:N/AC:L/Au:N/C:N/I:P/A:N"},"baseSeverity":"MEDIUM"}]},"configurations":[{"nodes":[{"operator":"OR","cpeMatch":[{"vulnerable":true,"criteria":"cpe:2.3:a:openbsd:openssh:8.2:*:*:*:*:*:*:*"}]}]}]}
{"id":"CVE-2023-25136","lastModified":"2026-10-14T23:17:15.010","vulnStatus":"Modified","descriptions":[{"lang":"en","value":"OpenSSH server (sshd) 9.1 introduced a double-free vulnerability during options.kex_algorithms handling. This is fixed in OpenSSH 9.2. The double free can be leveraged, by an unauthenticated remote attacker in the default configuration, to jump to any location in the sshd address space. One third-party report states \"remote code execution is theoretically possible.\""}],"metrics":{"cvssMetricV31":[{"type":"Primary","cvssData":{"baseScore":6.5,"baseSeverity":"MEDIUM","vectorString":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:H"}}]},"configurations":[{"nodes":[{"operator":"OR","cpeMatch":[{"vulnerable":true,"criteria":"cpe:2.3:a:openbsd:openssh:9.1:*:*:*:*:*:*:*"}]}]},{"nodes":[{"operator":"OR","cpeMatch":[{"vulnerable":true,"criteria":"cpe:2.3:o:fedoraproject:fedora:37:*:*:*:*:*:*:*"},{"vulnerable":true,"criteria":"cpe:2.3:o:fedoraproject:fedora:38:*:*:*:*:*:*:*"}]}]},{"nodes":[{"operator":"OR","cpeMatch":[{"vulnerable":true,"criteria":"cpe:2.3:a:netapp:ontap_select_deploy_administration_utility:-:*:*:*:*:*:*:*"}]}]},{"operator":"AND","nodes":[{"operator":"OR","cpeMatch":[{"vulnerable":true,"criteria":"cpe:2.3:o:netapp:a250_firmware:-:*:*:*:*:*:*:*"}]},{"operator":"OR","cpeMatch":[{"vulnerable":false,"criteria":"cpe:2.3:h:netapp:a250:-:*:*:*:*:*:*:*"}]}]},{"operator":"AND","nodes":[{"operator":"OR","cpeMatch":[{"vulnerable":true,"criteria":"cpe:2.3:o:netapp:500f_firmware:-:*:*:*:*:*:*:*"}]},{"operator":"OR","cpeMatch":[{"vulnerable":false,"criteria":"cpe:2.3:h:netapp:500f:-:*:*:*:*:*:*:*"}]}]},{"operator":"AND","nodes":[{"operator":"OR","cpeMatch":[{"vulnerable":true,"criteria":"cpe:2.3:o:netapp:c250_firmware:-:*:*:*:*:*:*:*"}]},{"operator":"OR","cpeMatch":[{"vulnerable":false,"criteria":"cpe:2.3:h:netapp:c250:-:*:*:*:*:*:*:*"}]}]}]}
{"id":"CVE-2026-10723","lastModified":"2026-11-02T17:48:44.730","vulnStatus":"Analyzed","descriptions":[{"lang":"en","value":"BIND may accept incorrect child-zone NSEC3 records as valid, which could allow an attacker to forge authenticated NXDOMAIN responses.\nThis issue affects BIND 9 versions 9.18.0 through 9.18.50, 9.20.0 through 9.20.24, 9.21.0 through 9.21.23, 9.11.3-S1 through 9.18.50-S1, and 9.20.9-S1 through 9.20.24-S1."}],"metrics":{"cvssMetricV31":[{"type":"Secondary","cvssData":{"baseScore":6.8,"baseSeverity":"MEDIUM","vectorString":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:N/I:H/A:N"}}]},"configurations":[{"nodes":[{"operator":"OR","cpeMatch":[{"vulnerable":true,"criteria":"cpe:2.3:a:isc:bind:*:*:*:*:supported_preview:*:*:*","versionStartIncluding":"9.11.3","versionEndIncluding":"9.18.50"},{"vulnerable":true,"criteria":"cpe:2.3:a:isc:bind:*:*:*:*:-:*:*:*","versionStartIncluding":"9.18.0","versionEndIncluding":"9.18.50"},{"vulnerable":true,"criteria":"cpe:2.3:a:isc:bind:*:*:*:*:-:*:*:*","versionStartIncluding":"9.20.0","versionEndIncluding":"9.20.24"},{"vulnerable":true,"criteria":"cpe:2.3:a:isc:bind:*:*:*:*:supported_preview:*:*:*","versionStartIncluding":"9.20.9","versionEndIncluding":"9.20.24"},{"vulnerable":true,"criteria":"cpe:2.3:a:isc:bind:*:*:*:*:-:*:*:*","versionStartIncluding":"9.21.0","versionEndIncluding":"9.21.23"}]}]}]}
{"id":"CVE-2026-123158","lastModified":"2026-11-10T13:48:52.110","vulnStatus":"Analyzed","descriptions":[{"lang":"en","value":"sshd in OpenSSH before 10.6p2 on Linux, when musl libc is used without PAM, lacks a workaround for a password authentication bypass (related to misinterpretation of whether a string is intended to be a password hash). For some configurations of accounts, any password between 256 and 1024 characters succeeds. An example of a platform using musl libc without PAM is Alpine Linux."}],"metrics":{"cvssMetricV31":[{"type":"Secondary","cvssData":{"baseScore":8.1,"baseSeverity":"HIGH","vectorString":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H"}}]},"configurations":[{"operator":"AND","nodes":[{"operator":"OR","cpeMatch":[{"vulnerable":true,"criteria":"cpe:2.3:a:openbsd:openssh:*:*:*:*:*:*:*:*","versionEndExcluding":"10.6"},{"vulnerable":true,"criteria":"cpe:2.3:a:openbsd:openssh:10.6:-:*:*:*:*:*:*"},{"vulnerable":true,"criteria":"cpe:2.3:a:openbsd:openssh:10.6:p1:*:*:*:*:*:*"}]},{"operator":"OR","cpeMatch":[{"vulnerable":false,"criteria":"cpe:2.3:o:alpinelinux:alpine_linux:*:*:*:*:*:*:*:*","versionEndExcluding":"3.21.10"},{"vulnerable":false,"criteria":"cpe:2.3:o:alpinelinux:alpine_linux:*:*:*:*:*:*:*:*","versionStartIncluding":"3.22.0","versionEndExcluding":"3.22.8"},{"vulnerable":false,"criteria":"cpe:2.3:o:alpinelinux:alpine_linux:*:*:*:*:*:*:*:*","versionStartIncluding":"3.23.0","versionEndExcluding":"3.23.8"},{"vulnerable":false,"criteria":"cpe:2.3:o:alpinelinux:alpine_linux:*:*:*:*:*:*:*:*","versionStartIncluding":"3.24.0","versionEndExcluding":"3.24.4"}]}]}]}
